How it works
At a high level, Delaunay32:
translates coordinates by the input minima and certifies predicate widths;
generates Morton keys and radix-sorts the sites;
constructs small divide-and-conquer leaves using exact orientation and in-circle predicates;
merges neighboring triangulations through compact primal edge rings;
optionally recovers constrained segments with in-place edge flips and legalizes every unconstrained edge;
optionally flood-fills polygon exteriors and holes without crossing their constrained boundaries;
marks the outer face and materializes indices that are counterclockwise in the triangulation coordinates.
For large inputs, radix sorting, independent subtrees, merge levels, and triangle export share a retained worker team. Small inputs stay serial to avoid synchronization overhead.
